# The one inventory of `data/seed/*.lino`, shared by every production path.
#
# Issue #991 moved it here. `src/seed/embedded.rs` and `src/web/seed_loader.js`
# each held this inventory as a hand-ordered list, and between them needed 41
# manual conflict resolutions -- two branches adding a seed file always appended
# to the same lines. Both files are now generated from this one, which is
# `merge=union` and sorted by name, so two branches adding a seed file produce
# two `seed` blocks in any order, the union keeps both, and
# `rust-script scripts/generate-seed-registry.rs --write` restores the order and
# rewrites the generated files.
#
# The flags, all of them optional.
#   bundle true       the file is embedded in the binary and joins the merged
#                     seed bundle returned by `seed_files()`
#   lexicon meaning   the file joins `MEANING_FILES` (the meaning lexicon)
#   lexicon response  the file joins `RESPONSE_FILES` (multilingual responses)
#   web true          the browser worker fetches the file at startup
#
# A file with `bundle` or `lexicon` gets an `include_str!` constant; a file with
# only `web` is fetched by the browser and never embedded.
#
# Two rules the canonical Links Notation parser imposes on this header, both
# enforced by `tests/unit/data_files.rs`. A comment line may not contain a colon,
# which the parser reads as structure, and no blank line may separate the header
# from `seed_registry`, which would end the document before it starts.
seed_registry
  seed agent-info
    bundle true
    web true
  seed agentic-tool-capabilities
    bundle true
  seed brainstorm-seeds
    bundle true
    web true
